{"timestamp":"2026-09-07T23:36:38.167Z","ordinal":19754,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a055ce-e4d9-77c1-ac18-0944a8c71200","turn_id":"01a07e3a-7088-74f3-8263-cbdd479f00a0","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-62ec9b03-b8f0-480c-bcee-48fd8fc8a55f","process_id":"30870","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","git -C .worktrees/issue-142-l10n diff --stat; git -C .worktrees/issue-143-search diff --stat; git -C .worktrees/search-clear-cancellation diff --stat; cat /private/tmp/cakebrew-142-ui.Bwegyu/review.md; cat /private/tmp/cakebrew-search-clear-fix.fdjddj/handoff.md"],"cwd":"file:///Users/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/cakebrew","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git -C .worktrees/issue-142-l10n diff --stat; git -C .worktrees/issue-143-search diff --stat; git -C .worktrees/search-clear-cancellation diff --stat; cat /private/tmp/cakebrew-142-ui.Bwegyu/review.md; cat /private/tmp/cakebrew-search-clear-fix.fdjddj/handoff.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":" .github/workflows/ci.yml                   | 6 ++++++\n AGENTS.md                                  | 5 +++++\n Cakebrew/de.lproj/Localizable.strings      | 1 -\n Cakebrew/fr.lproj/Localizable.strings      | 1 -\n Cakebrew/it.lproj/Localizable.strings      | 1 -\n Cakebrew/pt.lproj/Localizable.strings      | 1 -\n Cakebrew/zh-Hans.lproj/Localizable.strings | 1 -\n 7 files changed, 11 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)\n Cakebrew.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj              | 14 ++++++\n Cakebrew/Controllers/BPHomebrewViewController.m | 59 +++++++++++--------------\n CakebrewUITests/CakebrewUITests.m               | 19 ++++++--\n 3 files changed, 54 insertions(+), 38 deletions(-)\n Cakebrew.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj              | 14 ++++++\n Cakebrew/Controllers/BPHomebrewViewController.m | 59 +++++++++++--------------\n CakebrewUITests/CakebrewUITests.m               | 19 ++++++--\n 3 files changed, 54 insertions(+), 38 deletions(-)\n# Independent #142 bounded UI review — APPROVED\n\nReviewed the entire branch/workspace diff and all untracked files under `.worktrees/issue-142-l10n` against main/HEAD after reading its complete AGENTS.md and cakebrew-ui-review. No source edits or commits. Source hash before and after: `c39d734d72e5298ba5ea7d4a7a4f2ccb8812d48d285475e63ef6a430ab743064`.\n\nNo actionable UI findings in this slice. Approval covers the restored Formulae translations, native presentation/accessibility, and report presentation; it is NOT full verification or a passing UI journey suite.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Isolated Debug build: `xcodebuild build -workspace Cakebrew.xcworkspace -scheme Cakebrew -configuration Debug -destination 'platform=macOS' -derivedDataPath /private/tmp/cakebrew-142-ui.Bwegyu/DerivedData CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=NO`. Host build passed in 13.824s; no warning/error lines. Initial sandbox attempt exited 66 before loading the existing valid workspace, with CoreSimulator/XPC errors; no source/config change used to overcome it.\n- Display unlocked before launch (`IOConsoleLocked = No`). Exclusive display/app/preferences/cache ownership granted by root. No XCUITest launched or retried.\n- Serialized exact temporary mock executable, `-BPMockBrew -BPLastSelectedSidebarRow 1 -BPSortColumnIdentifier '' -AppleLanguages '(locale)'`, for de/fr/it/pt/zh-Hans. Runtime `NSBundle.mainBundle.preferredLocalizations` confirmed each requested locale, recorded in `*-light-debugger.log`. Exact owned PIDs: de24710, fr25940, it26542, pt26791, zh-Hans27006.\n- Native app-open-URLs flow: `open -a <exact temporary app> <temporary Brewfile>` containing only `brew 'mockwget'` and `cask 'mockchrome'`. Review sheet presented without confirming installation. Mock fixture rows/badges verified in AX and screenshots. No real Homebrew/package operations.\n- Correct table AX descriptions and review section headings: de `Formeln`, fr `Formules`, it `Formule`, pt `Fórmulas`, zh-Hans unchanged `Formulae`. Main/review AX dumps for each locale preserve `brewfile.review.entries` and sidebar stable identifiers. Native AXTextArea exposes full readable review text; native sheet and buttons remain intact.\n- Visually inspected ten app-window-only PNGs: `de/fr/it/pt/zh-Hans-system.png` (actual system Dark Aqua) and matching `*-aqua.png`. Restored headings fit comfortably, no truncation/clipping/overlap or contrast regression. Sidebar badges retain expected mock counts. Existing long French/Italian sidebar strings abbreviate with ellipsis; their keys/layout are unchanged by this slice and full AX descriptions remain available.\n- Opposite-appearance check was a diagnostic-only temporary `NSApp.appearance = NSAppearance(named: NSAppearanceNameAqua)` through LLDB against the exact owned PID, detached before capture; original appearance was nil and restored to nil. No global appearance or language settings changed. This is not evidence of physical typing, menu navigation, or UI-journey execution.\n- Review sheets cancelled via existing AppKit endSheet returnCode1001, then owned apps quit normally; no install confirmation. First German cancellation diagnostic had a compile-only expression error for untyped attachedSheet; explicit NSWindow cast corrected it. No product change. A capture helper initially stopped when the French window was not yet on-screen; existing mock was retained, readiness verified, then capture continued. Neither event was a failed application test.\n- Report reviewed from real Markdown output plus renderer: semantic heading hierarchy and labeled summary table; counts distinguish confirmed placeholders, intentional English, unreviewed equality, different, missing, and extra. Informational/non-blocking nature and non-quality nature of Different explicitly stated. Sorted, escaped key lists provide exact actionable identities without color-dependent meaning. JSON alternative available. Report is lengthy by design; no actionable presentation problem. GitHub's live rendering/assistive-technology implementation was not exercised, because no PR/job publication is authorized in this review.\n\n## State restoration and limitations\n\nFresh backup immediately before first launch contained six persistent preference keys, not an older run's backup. After every owned mock had exited, exact persistent domain restored and independently re-read in a fresh process: six keys equal. Cache restored byte-for-byte, SHA256 `01c1e93bc5bc2541d18a2d5711497c2290c13a0163d269d510bc2ae15a016df0`. Backups retained here as evidence. Temporary Brewfile and helper source/input scripts removed after completion; no scratch files added to the repository. No installed app modified and no unrelated processes terminated.\n\nNative regression evidence in implementer handoff covers runtime resource values. Existing Brewfile journey `testBrewfileReviewShowsGroupedStatusesAndCancelRunsNothing` covers grouped review/cancel, but was not run here. Previously reported XCTest initialization failures remain unresolved and must not be described as UI test passes. Complete verification and subsequent independent code review remain separate gates.\n# Separate queued-search cancellation fix\n\nWorktree: /Users/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/cakebrew/.worktrees/search-clear-cancellation\nBranch: fix/search-clear-cancellation. Base: 8263716 plus the primary agent's uncommitted copy of the frozen #143 refactor.\n\nOwned and changed ONLY Cakebrew/Controllers/BPSearchCoordinator.m and CakebrewTests/BPSearchCoordinatorTests.m relative to that refactor. No commit, staging, push or PR.\n\n## Separate TDD evidence\n\nAdded two regression tests first, before changing production code:\n\n- testClearingSearchInvalidatesRetainedCallbackWithoutResumingSearch schedules work, clears search before manually firing the retained block, then asserts zero searches and no resumed search state. The injected search action simulates delivering results so the state assertion proves the stale work cannot reopen search.\n- testNewQueryRunsAfterClearingWithoutRevivingOlderQuery queues an old query, clears, queues a fresh query, explicitly executes both retained callbacks, and requires only the fresh query to run. Its results can start a new session and restore its sidebar row normally.\n\nRED: red.log:1605-1618 contains four expected assertion failures across the two new tests: performed=1 instead of0, searching unexpectedly true, stale query still executing after a new query, and performed containing old plus new instead of new only. All six original coordinator tests passed. Eight tests executed, four assertion failures, xcodebuild exit65. This is an observed behavioral regression failure, not a compile or runner error.\n\nMinimal fix: increment generation once at the start of endSearchReturningSidebarRow, before canceling in-flight manager work and returning the saved sidebar row. Existing queued callbacks already compare their captured generation. No extra scheduler, rendering, manager, toolbar, sidebar, UI, or state-restoration changes.\n\nGREEN status and command completion are recorded in the final section below; do not assume green from the source change alone.\n\nFocused command: xcodebuild test -workspace Cakebrew.xcworkspace -scheme CakebrewTests -destination 'platform=macOS' -derivedDataPath /private/tmp/cakebrew-search-clear-fix.fdjddj/DerivedData -only-testing:CakebrewTests/BPSearchCoordinatorTests CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=NO.\n\n## Frozen scope and hashes\n\nfix-only.patch contains exactly the two-file delta: one production line and42 test lines. It applies cleanly with git apply --check to the original refactor worktree; its reverse applies cleanly to this fix worktree. Dry-run checks only, neither application performed.\n\nFix-only patch SHA256: 51601f23a2843677e83acccef8a7a32bf9570f4f5e9e9c6cfa868b42270a6c88\n\nCombined full source SHA256: 3770617bd4179ccb8dd50761b5cf9b33730589c5591dae1e1016a06becad8daa\n\nFull source hashing uses git diff HEAD --binary bytes, then s