{"timestamp":"2026-09-07T23:51:16.738Z","ordinal":20171,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0229170f3e6ec7c3016a9f4df340d887d1b0be80e9fae420cf","status":"completed","call_id":"call_Z7VjP9n5T7EE05UtHSEUuncG","name":"exec","input":"text(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"gh issue view 142 --repo scottdensmore/cakebrew --json number,title,body,state; gh issue view 143 --repo scottdensmore/cakebrew --json number,title,body,state\",\"sandbox_permissions\":\"require_escalated\",\"justification\":\"May I read the two GitHub issues to check the final verification and review against their acceptance criteria?\",\"max_output_tokens\":4000}));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a07e3a-7088-74f3-8263-cbdd479f00a0","create_time":1788825073.577031}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-07T23:51:16.919Z","ordinal":20172,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a055ce-e4d9-77c1-ac18-0944a8c71200","turn_id":"01a07e3a-7088-74f3-8263-cbdd479f00a0","session_id":"01a055ce-e4d9-77c1-ac18-0944a8c71200","root_turn_id":"01a07e3a-7088-74f3-8263-cbdd479f00a0","response_id":"resp_0229170f3e6ec7c3016a9f4df1548c87d1b82ab882fe408143","usage":{"input_tokens":96815,"cached_input_tokens":96384,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":103,"reasoning_output_tokens":0,"total_tokens":96918},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":4558279,"cached_input_tokens":4495872,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":6547,"reasoning_output_tokens":1857,"total_tokens":4564826},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":267201650,"cached_input_tokens":263651072,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":514988,"reasoning_output_tokens":186013,"total_tokens":267716638}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-07T23:51:20.583Z","ordinal":20173,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a055ce-e4d9-77c1-ac18-0944a8c71200","turn_id":"01a07e3a-7088-74f3-8263-cbdd479f00a0","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-fc6d29b2-d700-48d4-b735-6d7a79862e68","process_id":"32690","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","gh issue view 142 --repo scottdensmore/cakebrew --json number,title,body,state; gh issue view 143 --repo scottdensmore/cakebrew --json number,title,body,state"],"cwd":"file:///Users/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/cakebrew","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"gh issue view 142 --repo scottdensmore/cakebrew --json number,title,body,state; gh issue view 143 --repo scottdensmore/cakebrew --json number,title,body,state"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"{\"body\":\"## Problem\\n\\nThe README advertises six localizations. In practice a German, French, Italian, Portuguese or Chinese user sees roughly a third of the interface in English.\\n\\nCounting only multi-word English sentences that appear verbatim in a non-English `.strings` file — so proper nouns and genuinely-identical words like \\\"Name\\\", \\\"Status\\\", \\\"Doctor\\\" are excluded — out of **184** keys:\\n\\n| Locale | Untranslated sentences |\\n|---|---|\\n| `de` | 35 |\\n| `fr` | 34 |\\n| `it` | 35 |\\n| `pt` | 36 |\\n| `zh-Hans` | 45 |\\n\\nNo keys are *missing* — `BPLocalizationParityTests` guarantees that, and it passes. They are present with the English text, which is exactly what AGENTS.md prescribes for a new string: *\\\"New strings use the English text in every locale until translated.\\\"*\\n\\nThat rule is right — it keeps `NSLocalizedString` from returning a raw key on screen — but nothing ever converts the placeholder into a translation, so the debt only grows. Every feature added recently contributed: the empty states, the cleanup preview, the Dock menu, the reload status lines, the Brewfile prompts.\\n\\nSample from `de.lproj`:\\n\\n```\\nEmpty_Search_Message        No formula or cask matches your search.\\nEmpty_Outdated_Title        Everything Is Up to Date\\nConfirmation_Cleanup        Homebrew will permanently remove %1$@, freeing about %2$@…\\nLoading_Status_AllCasks     Fetching the cask catalog — this can take a minute the first time…\\nDock_Show_Outdated          Show Outdated Formulae\\n```\\n\\n## Proposal\\n\\nTwo separable pieces:\\n\\n1. **Make the debt visible.** A test or CI step that reports the untranslated count per locale — not failing the build, because the English-placeholder rule deliberately allows it, but printing a number that someone can watch. Without this, nobody can tell a placeholder from a translation that happens to match.\\n2. **Translate the backlog.** Roughly 35 sentences per locale. Homebrew terms (\\\"Casks\\\", \\\"Brewfile\\\", \\\"tap\\\") stay untranslated by existing convention.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n\\n- [ ] A per-locale untranslated count is reported somewhere a maintainer will see it\\n- [ ] Placeholder entries are distinguishable from deliberate matches — a marker comment, a separate file section, or a documented allow-list for legitimately identical strings\\n- [ ] The English-placeholder rule in AGENTS.md gains a pointer to wherever the debt is tracked\\n\\n## Notes\\n\\n`plutil -lint` each file after editing. `BPLocalizationParityTests` already guards against a key going missing entirely — this is the complementary gap, and it is invisible to that test by construction.\",\"number\":142,\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"title\":\"A third of the UI is untranslated in every non-English locale\"}\n{\"body\":\"## Problem\\n\\n`Cakebrew/Controllers/BPHomebrewViewController.m` is **1374 lines** and **62 methods**, conforming to **seven** protocols:\\n\\n```objc\\n@interface BPHomebrewViewController () <NSTableViewDelegate,\\nBPSideBarControllerDelegate,\\nBPSelectedFormulaViewControllerDelegate,\\nBPHomebrewManagerDelegate,\\nBPToolbarProtocol,\\nNSMenuDelegate,\\nNSOpenSavePanelDelegate>\\n```\\n\\nIts `#pragma mark` sections show what has accumulated: footer label, homebrew-manager delegate, search mode, table-view delegate, two more delegates, menu delegate, **IBActions (lines 875–1365 — 490 lines on its own)**, and open/save panel delegate.\\n\\nIt is the junction for the sidebar, the table, the detail pane, search, the toolbar, the Dock menu, Brewfile import, reload progress, cancel, and every user operation. Recent work made this worse rather than better — the Dock menu (#133), Brewfile import (#136), reload progress (#138) and the reload Stop control (#139) each added another responsibility to this one file.\\n\\nIt also has **no direct test coverage**. It is the largest source file in the project and the only one of that size that nothing exercises directly:\\n\\n| File | Lines | Covered |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| `BPHomebrewViewController.m` | 1374 | no |\\n| `BPHomebrewInterface.m` | 997 | yes |\\n| `BPSideBarController.m` | 610 | yes |\\n| `BPHomebrewManager.m` | 560 | yes |\\n\\nThe reason nothing tests it is circular: it is not in the `CakebrewTests` target, because pulling it in drags the whole UI object graph along. So its logic is only reachable through ~8-minute UI journeys.\\n\\n## Proposal\\n\\nExtract along the seams the `#pragma mark` sections already suggest, in separate thin slices — not one big move:\\n\\n- **Operations** (install / uninstall / upgrade / pin / tap / cleanup / import / export confirmations and dispatch) into a coordinator that owns the confirmation sheets and the operation window.\\n- **Search** (`BPTimedDispatch` coalescing, restore-row-on-clear) into its own controller.\\n- **Reload presentation** (`didPublishListForMode:`, `didBeginStepForMode:`, reveal, empty state) into a presenter.\\n- Leave the view controller owning the view hierarchy and delegate plumbing.\\n\\nEach extracted piece becomes unit-testable, which is the actual payoff.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n\\n- [ ] `BPHomebrewViewController.m` is meaningfully smaller and no longer the junction for unrelated features\\n- [ ] At least one extracted collaborator is in the `CakebrewTests` target with direct tests\\n- [ ] Every existing UI journey still passes — this is behaviour-preserving\\n- [ ] Each extraction is its own PR\\n\\n## Notes\\n\\nThis is a behaviour-changing refactor only in structure, so per AGENTS.md the tests come first: characterise the behaviour being moved with a test against the *new* seam, watch it fail, then move the code. The 41 UI journeys are the safety net for the parts that cannot be unit-tested — run them on every slice, not just the last.\",\"number\":143,\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"title\":\"Decompose BPHomebrewViewController — 1374 lines, 62 methods, 7 protocols\"}\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"{\"body\":\"## Problem\\n\\nThe README advertises six localizations. In practice a German, French, Italian, Portuguese or Chinese user sees roughly a third of the interface in English.\\n\\nCounting only multi-word English sentences that appear verbatim in a non-English `.strings` file — so proper nouns and genuinely-identical words like \\\"Name\\\", \\\"Status\\\", \\\"Doctor\\\" are excluded — out of **184** keys:\\n\\n| Locale | Untranslated sentences |\\n|---|---|\\n| `de` | 35 |\\n| `fr` | 34 |\\n| `it` | 35 |\\n| `pt` | 36 |\\n| `zh-Hans` | 45 |\\n\\nNo keys are *missing* — `BPLocalizationParityTests` guarantees that, and it passes. They are present with the English text, which is exactly what AGENTS.md prescribes for a new string: *\\\"New strings use the English text in every locale until translated.\\\"*\\n\\nThat rule is right — it keeps `NSLocalizedString` from returning a raw key on screen — but nothing ever converts the placeholder into a translation, so the debt only grows. Every feature added recently contributed: the empty states, the cleanup preview, the Dock menu, the reload status lines, the Brewfile prompts.\\n\\nSample from `de.lproj`:\\n\\n```\\nEmpty_Search_Message        No formula or cask matches your search.\\nEmpty_Outdated_Title        Everything Is Up to Date\\nConfirmation_Cleanup        Homebrew will permanently remove %1$@, freeing about %2$@…\\nLoading_Status_AllCasks     Fetching the cask catalog — this can take a minute the first time…\\nDock_Show_Outdated          Show Outdated Formulae\\n```\\n\\n## Proposal\\n\\nTwo separable pieces:\\n\\n1. **Make the debt visible.** A test or CI step that reports the untranslated count per locale — not failing the build, because the English-placeholder rule deliberately allows it, but printing a number that someone can watch. Without this, nobody can tell a placeholder from a translation that happens to match.\\n2. **Translate the backlog.** Roughly 35 sentences per locale. Homebrew terms (\\\"Casks\\\", \\\"Brewfile\\\", \\\"tap\\\") stay untranslated by existing convention.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n\\n- [ ] A per-locale untranslated count is reported somewhere a maintainer will see it\\n- [ ] Placeholder entries are distinguishable from deliberate matches — a marker comment, a separate file section, or a documented allow-list for legitimately identical strings\\n- [ ] The English-placeholder rule in AGENTS.md gains a pointer to wherever the debt is tracked\\n\\n## Notes\\n\\n`plutil -lint` each file after editing. `BPLocalizationParityTests` already guards against a key going missing entirely — this is the complementary gap, and it is invisible to that test by construction.\",\"number\":142,\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"title\":\"A third of the UI is untranslated in every non-English locale\"}\n{\"body\":\"## Problem\\n\\n`Cakebrew/Controllers/BPHomebrewViewController.m` is **1374 lines** and **62 methods**, conforming to **seven** protocols:\\n\\n```objc\\n@interface BPHomebrewViewController () <NSTableViewDelegate,\\nBPSideBarControllerDelegate,\\nBPSelectedFormulaViewControllerDelegate,\\nBPHomebrewManagerDelegate,\\nBPToolbarProtocol,\\nNSMenuDelegate,\\nNSOpenSavePanelDelegate>\\n```\\n\\nIts `#pragma mark` sections show what has accumulated: footer label, homebrew-manager delegate, search mode, table-view delegate, two more delegates, menu delegate, **IBActions (lines 875–1365 — 490 lines on its own)**, and open/save panel delegate.\\n\\nIt is the junction for the sidebar, the table, the detail pane, search, the toolbar, the Dock menu, Brewfile import, reload progress, cancel, and every user operation. Recent work made this worse rather than better — the Dock menu (#133), Brewfile import (#136), reload progress (#138) and the reload Stop control (#139) each added another responsibility to this one file.\\n\\nIt also has **no direct test coverage**. It is the largest source file in the project and the only one of that size that nothing exercises directly:\\n\\n| File | Lines | Covered |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| `BPHomebrewViewController.m` | 1374 | no |\\n| `BPHomebrewInterface.m` | 997 | yes |\\n| `BPSideBarController.m` | 610 | yes |\\n| `BPHomebrewManager.m` | 560 | yes |\\n\\nThe reason nothing tests it is circular: it is not in the `CakebrewTests` target, because pulling it in drags the whole UI object graph along. So its logic is only reachable through ~8-minute UI journeys.\\n\\n## Proposal\\n\\nExtract along the seams the `#pragma mark` sections already suggest, in separate thin slices — not one big move:\\n\\n- **Operations** (install / uninstall / upgrade / pin / tap / cleanup / import / export confirmations and dispatch) into a coordinator that owns the confirmation sheets and the operation window.\\n- **Search** (`BPTimedDispatch` coalescing, restore-row-on-clear) into its own controller.\\n- **Reload presentation** (`didPublishListForMode:`, `didBeginStepForMode:`, reveal, empty state) into a presenter.\\n- Leave the view controller owning the view hierarchy and delegate plumbing.\\n\\nEach extracted piece becomes unit-testable, which is the actual payoff.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n\\n- [ ] `BPHomebrewViewController.m` is meaningfully smaller and no longer the junction for unrelated features\\n- [ ] At least one extracted collaborator is in the `CakebrewTests` target with direct tests\\n- [ ] Every existing UI journey still passes — this is behaviour-preserving\\n- [ ] Each extraction is its own PR\\n\\n## Notes\\n\\nThis is a behaviour-changing refactor only in structure, so per AGENTS.md the tests come first: characterise the behaviour being moved with a test against the *new* seam, watch it fail, then move the code. The 41 UI journeys are the safety net for the parts that cannot be unit-tested — run them on every slice, not just the last.\",\"number\":143,\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"title\":\"Decompose BPHomebrewViewController — 1374 lines, 62 methods, 7 protocols\"}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":934785893},"formatted_output":"{\"body\":\"## Problem\\n\\nThe README advertises six localizations. In practice a German, French, Italian, Portuguese or Chinese user sees roughly a third of the interface in English.\\n\\nCounting only multi-word English sentences that appear verbatim in a non-English `.strings` file — so proper nouns and genuinely-identical words like \\\"Name\\\", \\\"Status\\\", \\\"Doctor\\\" are excluded — out of **184** keys:\\n\\n| Locale | Untranslated sentences |\\n|---|---|\\n| `de` | 35 |\\n| `fr` | 34 |\\n| `it` | 35 |\\n| `pt` | 36 |\\n| `zh-Hans` | 45 |\\n\\nNo keys are *missing* — `BPLocalizationParityTests` guarantees that, and it passes. They are present with the English text, which is exactly what AGENTS.md prescribes for a new string: *\\\"New strings use the English text in every locale until translated.\\\"*\\n\\nThat rule is right — it keeps `NSLocalizedString` from returning a raw key on screen — but nothing ever converts the placeholder into a translation, so the debt only grows. Every feature added recently contributed: the empty states, the cleanup preview, the Dock menu, the reload status lines, the Brewfile prompts.\\n\\nSample from `de.lproj`:\\n\\n```\\nEmpty_Search_Message        No formula or cask matches your search.\\nEmpty_Outdated_Title        Everything Is Up to Date\\nConfirmation_Cleanup        Homebrew will permanently remove %1$@, freeing about %2$@…\\nLoading_Status_AllCasks     Fetching the cask catalog — this can take a minute the first time…\\nDock_Show_Outdated          Show Outdated Formulae\\n```\\n\\n## Proposal\\n\\nTwo separable pieces:\\n\\n1. **Make the debt visible.** A test or CI step that reports the untranslated count per locale — not failing the build, because the English-placeholder rule deliberately allows it, but printing a number that someone can watch. Without this, nobody can tell a placeholder from a translation that happens to match.\\n2. **Translate the backlog.** Roughly 35 sentences per locale. Homebrew terms (\\\"Casks\\\", \\\"Brewfile\\\", \\\"tap\\\") stay untranslated by existing convention.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n\\n- [ ] A per-locale untranslated count is reported somewhere a maintainer will see it\\n- [ ] Placeholder entries are distinguishable from deliberate matches — a marker comment, a separate file section, or a documented allow-list for legitimately identical strings\\n- [ ] The English-placeholder rule in AGENTS.md gains a pointer to wherever the debt is tracked\\n\\n## Notes\\n\\n`plutil -lint` each file after editing. `BPLocalizationParityTests` already guards against a key going missing entirely — this is the complementary gap, and it is invisible to that test by construction.\",\"number\":142,\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"title\":\"A third of the UI is untranslated in every non-English locale\"}\n{\"body\":\"## Problem\\n\\n`Cakebrew/Controllers/BPHomebrewViewController.m` is **1374 lines** and **62 methods**, conforming to **seven** protocols:\\n\\n```objc\\n@interface BPHomebrewViewController () <NSTableViewDelegate,\\nBPSideBarControllerDelegate,\\nBPSelectedFormulaViewControllerDelegate,\\nBPHomebrewManagerDelegate,\\nBPToolbarProtocol,\\nNSMenuDelegate,\\nNSOpenSavePanelDelegate>\\n```\\n\\nIts `#pragma mark` sections show what has accumulated: footer label, homebrew-manager delegate, search mode, table-view delegate, two more delegates, menu delegate, **IBActions (lines 875–1365 — 490 lines on its own)**, and open/save panel delegate.\\n\\nIt is the junction for the sidebar, the table, the detail pane, search, the toolbar, the Dock menu, Brewfile import, reload progress, cancel, and every user operation. Recent work made this worse rather than better — the Dock menu (#133), Brewfile import (#136), reload progress (#138) and the reload Stop control (#139) each added another responsibility to this one file.\\n\\nIt also has **no direct test coverage**. It is the largest source file in the project and the only one of that size that nothing exercises directly:\\n\\n| File | Lines | Covered |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| `BPHomebrewViewController.m` | 1374 | no |\\n| `BPHomebrewInterface.m` | 997 | yes |\\n| `BPSideBarController.m` | 610 | yes |\\n| `BPHomebrewManager.m` | 560 | yes |\\n\\nThe reason nothing tests it is circular: it is not in the `CakebrewTests` target, because pulling it in drags the whole UI object graph along. So its logic is only reachable through ~8-minute UI journeys.\\n\\n## Proposal\\n\\nExtract along the seams the `#pragma mark` sections already suggest, in separate thin slices — not one big move:\\n\\n- **Operations** (install / uninstall / upgrade / pin / tap / cleanup / import / export confirmations and dispatch) into a coordinator that owns the confirmation sheets and the operation window.\\n- **Search** (`BPTimedDispatch` coalescing, restore-row-on-clear) into its own controller.\\n- **Reload presentation** (`didPublishListForMode:`, `didBeginStepForMode:`, reveal, empty state) into a presenter.\\n- Leave the view controller owning the view hierarchy and delegate plumbing.\\n\\nEach extracted piece becomes unit-testable, which is the actual payoff.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n\\n- [ ] `BPHomebrewViewController.m` is meaningfully smaller and no longer the junction for unrelated features\\n- [ ] At least one extracted collaborator is in the `CakebrewTests` target with direct tests\\n- [ ] Every existing UI journey still passes — this is behaviour-preserving\\n- [ ] Each extraction is its own PR\\n\\n## Notes\\n\\nThis is a behaviour-changing refactor only in structure, so per AGENTS.md the tests come first: characterise the behaviour being moved with a test against the *new* seam, watch it fail, then move the code. The 41 UI journeys are the safety net for the parts that cannot be unit-tested — run them on every slice, not just the last.\",\"number\":143,\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"title\":\"Decompose BPHomebrewViewController — 1374 lines, 62 methods, 7 protocols\"}\n"},"started_at_ms":1788825079647,"completed_at_ms":1788825080582}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-07T23:51:20.690Z","ordinal":20174,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a07e48-9372-72a0-ac12-f54f819bbd37","call_id":"call_Z7VjP9n5T7EE05UtHSEUuncG","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.9 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"be9593\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.934806647,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":1463,\"output\":\"{\\\"body\\\":\\\"## Problem\\\\n\\\\nThe README advertises six localizations. In practice a German, French, Italian, Portuguese or Chinese user sees roughly a third of the interface in English.\\\\n\\\\nCounting only multi-word English sentences that appear verbatim in a non-English `.strings` file — so proper nouns and genuinely-identical words like \\\\\\\"Name\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Status\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Doctor\\\\\\\" are excluded — out of **184** keys:\\\\n\\\\n| Locale | Untranslated sentences |\\\\n|---|---|\\\\n| `de` | 35 |\\\\n| `fr` | 34 |\\\\n| `it` | 35 |\\\\n| `pt` | 36 |\\\\n| `zh-Hans` | 45 |\\\\n\\\\nNo keys are *missing* — `BPLocalizationParityTests` guarantees that, and it passes. They are present with the English text, which is exactly what AGENTS.md prescribes for a new string: *\\\\\\\"New strings use the English text in every locale until translated.\\\\\\\"*\\\\n\\\\nThat rule is right — it keeps `NSLocalizedString` from returning a raw key on screen — but nothing ever converts the placeholder into a translation, so the debt only grows. Every feature added recently contributed: the empty states, the cleanup preview, the Dock menu, the reload status lines, the Brewfile prompts.\\\\n\\\\nSample from `de.lproj`:\\\\n\\\\n```\\\\nEmpty_Search_Message        No formula or cask matches your search.\\\\nEmpty_Outdated_Title        Everything Is Up to Date\\\\nConfirmation_Cleanup        Homebrew will permanently remove %1$@, freeing about %2$@…\\\\nLoading_Status_AllCasks     Fetching the cask catalog — this can take a minute the first time…\\\\nDock_Show_Outdated          Show Outdated Formulae\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n## Proposal\\\\n\\\\nTwo separable pieces:\\\\n\\\\n1. **Make the debt visible.** A test or CI step that reports the untranslated count per locale — not failing the build, because the English-placeholder rule deliberately allows it, but printing a number that someone can watch. Without this, nobody can tell a placeholder from a translation that happens to match.\\\\n2. **Translate the backlog.** Roughly 35 sentences per locale. Homebrew terms (\\\\\\\"Casks\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Brewfile\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"tap\\\\\\\") stay untranslated by existing convention.\\\\n\\\\n## Acceptance criteria\\\\n\\\\n- [ ] A per-locale untranslated count is reported somewhere a maintainer will see it\\\\n- [ ] Placeholder entries are distinguishable from deliberate matches — a marker comment, a separate file section, or a documented allow-list for legitimately identical strings\\\\n- [ ] The English-placeholder rule in AGENTS.md gains a pointer to wherever the debt is tracked\\\\n\\\\n## Notes\\\\n\\\\n`plutil -lint` each file after editing. `BPLocalizationParityTests` already guards against a key going missing entirely — this is the complementary gap, and it is invisible to that test by construction.\\\",\\\"number\\\":142,\\\"state\\\":\\\"OPEN\\\",\\\"title\\\":\\\"A third of the UI is untranslated in every non-English locale\\\"}\\n{\\\"body\\\":\\\"## Problem\\\\n\\\\n`Cakebrew/Controllers/BPHomebrewViewController.m` is **1374 lines** and **62 methods**, conforming to **seven** protocols:\\\\n\\\\n```objc\\\\n@interface BPHomebrewViewController () <NSTableViewDelegate,\\\\nBPSideBarControllerDelegate,\\\\nBPSelectedFormulaViewControllerDelegate,\\\\nBPHomebrewManagerDelegate,\\\\nBPToolbarProtocol,\\\\nNSMenuDelegate,\\\\nNSOpenSavePanelDelegate>\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nIts `#pragma mark` sections show what has accumulated: footer label, homebrew-manager delegate, search mode, table-view delegate, two more delegates, menu delegate, **IBActions (lines 875–1365 — 490 lines on its own)**, and open/save panel delegate.\\\\n\\\\nIt is the junction for the sidebar, the table, the detail pane, search, the toolbar, the Dock menu, Brewfile import, reload progress, cancel, and every user operation. Recent work made this worse rather than better — the Dock menu (#133), Brewfile import (#136), reload progress (#138) and the reload Stop control (#139) each added another responsibility to this one file.\\\\n\\\\nIt also has **no direct test coverage**. It is the largest source file in the project and the only one of that size that nothing exercises directly:\\\\n\\\\n| File | Lines | Covered |\\\\n|---|---|---|\\\\n| `BPHomebrewViewController.m` | 1374 | no |\\\\n| `BPHomebrewInterface.m` | 997 | yes |\\\\n| `BPSideBarController.m` | 610 | yes |\\\\n| `BPHomebrewManager.m` | 560 | yes |\\\\n\\\\nThe reason nothing tests it is circular: it is not in the `CakebrewTests` target, because pulling it in drags the whole UI object graph along. So its logic is only reachable through ~8-minute UI journeys.\\\\n\\\\n## Proposal\\\\n\\\\nExtract along the seams the `#pragma mark` sections already suggest, in separate thin slices — not one big move:\\\\n\\\\n- **Operations** (install / uninstall / upgrade / pin / tap / cleanup / import / export confirmations and dispatch) into a coordinator that owns the confirmation sheets and the operation window.\\\\n- **Search** (`BPTimedDispatch` coalescing, restore-row-on-clear) into its own controller.\\\\n- **Reload presentation** (`didPublishListForMode:`, `didBeginStepForMode:`, reveal, empty state) into a presenter.\\\\n- Leave the view controller owning the view hierarchy and delegate plumbing.\\\\n\\\\nEach extracted piece becomes unit-testable, which is the actual payoff.\\\\n\\\\n## Acceptance criteria\\\\n\\\\n- [ ] `BPHomebrewViewController.m` is meaningfully smaller and no longer the junction for unrelated features\\\\n- [ ] At least one extracted collaborator is in the `CakebrewTests` target with direct tests\\\\n- [ ] Every existing UI journey still passes — this is behaviour-preserving\\\\n- [ ] Each extraction is its own PR\\\\n\\\\n## Notes\\\\n\\\\nThis is a behaviour-changing refactor only in structure, so per AGENTS.md the tests come first: characterise the behaviour being moved with a test against the *new* seam, watch it fail, then move the code. The 41 UI journeys are the safety net for the parts that cannot be unit-tested — run them on every slice, not just the last.\\\",\\\"number\\\":143,\\\"state\\\":\\\"OPEN\\\",\\\"title\\\":\\\"Decompose BPHomebrewViewController — 1374 lines, 62 methods, 7 protocols\\\"}\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a07e3a-7088-74f3-8263-cbdd479f00a0","create_time":1788825080.690662}}}
