{"timestamp":"2026-09-08T00:10:32.707Z","ordinal":20612,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a07e5a-2783-7b42-8091-6c71262d4446","author":"/root/expert_review","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/expert_review\nPayload:\nP2 — Remove fixed live translation counts from the mandatory CI test. [localization-debt-tests.rb:177](</Users/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/cakebrew/.worktrees/issue-142-l10n/scripts/tests/localization-debt-tests.rb:177>) hard-codes 254 keys and per-locale English-match totals. Valid new strings or ordinary translations therefore fail CI before its informational report runs.\n\nRead-only input probes confirmed both cases: a valid added key produces 255; translating one unreviewed German value changes its total from 127 to 126. Use fixture expectations or count-partition invariants instead, retaining strict invalid-input/metadata checks.\n\nFull branch and staged, unstaged, and untracked files reviewed against frozen hash `c39d734…`; no other actionable findings. Source unchanged and released. Gate not approved: route this fix to the implementer, then obtain fresh full verification and code review.\n\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a07e3a-7088-74f3-8263-cbdd479f00a0","create_time":1788826232.707154}}}
