clean run, without retries.\n- Independent visual review covered all five affected locales in Aqua/Dark Aqua and accessibility; expert rereview approved after correcting the live-count test finding.\n\nAn earlier, superseded UI run had one Cursor-window interruption timeout, followed by a passing targeted retry. After the review correction, the entire verification sequence was repeated; the final full run above passed without a retry. No live GitHub summary rendering was claimed during local review; CI will exercise publication.\n\nRefs #142; the translation backlog remains separate.\n"},"/private/tmp/cakebrew-delivery.1XpoA7/search-refactor.md":{"type":"add","content":"## Summary\n\nExtract debounce, cancellation, and search-session state into a directly tested `BPSearchCoordinator`. The view controller retains rendering, row validation, and sidebar selection. This is the first small search slice of #143, not the full controller decomposition.\n\nThe cask-search UI journey now invokes search and waits for a nonmatching result to disappear before asserting the matching cask and preserved sidebar identity.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Observed absent-header compile failure before implementing the new seam, then six focused coordinator tests passed.\n- Warning-free Debug and Release builds; UI target compiled explicitly.\n- Full unit suite: 442 tests, zero failures, seven deliberate opt-in real-Homebrew compatibility skips.\n- Full UI suite: 76/76 passed in one clean final run, without retries.\n- Independent Aqua/Dark Aqua, accessibility, and expert code reviews approved the exact source.\n- Fresh preferences/cache restored exactly after tests; package-operation journeys use mock brew.\n\n## Scope and limitations\n\nThis preserves existing behavior. Queued searches surviving clear are addressed by the separate dependent fix PR. A distinct pre-existing completed-cask-search/same-row clearing display issue remains outside these slices. This does not claim a fix for that rendering behavior or complete issue #143.\n\nEarlier local automation startup attempts failed before tests began; after Xcode was closed, the final full gate above passed. No host permission or daemon changes were made.\n\nRefs #143.\n"},"/private/tmp/cakebrew-delivery.1XpoA7/search-clear.md":{"type":"add","content":"## Summary\n\nDependent on the search-coordinator refactor; this PR contains only the cancellation fix and its regression coverage.\n\nAdvance the generation before ending search so retained debounced work cannot repopulate a cleared search. New queries and notification navigation retain their existing behavior.\n\nAdd a DEBUG, explicitly mock-only native menu action that queues then clears via the actual toolbar text-change delegate in one main event. The new UI journey checks an empty field, retained Installed Formulae rows, and no late cask search result. Its title is present in all six locales.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Two unit regressions were observed red before the generation fix, then green.\n- UI mutation proof: removing only the clear-generation guard left stale mockvscode results under an empty field and made the positive installed-row assertion fail; restoring the guard passed the identical journey. The inverted AX expectation alone did not catch the mutation and is not credited as the biting assertion.\n- Warning-free Debug/Release builds and explicit UI-target compilation; all six strings lints passed.\n- Full unit suite: 444 tests, zero failures, seven deliberate opt-in real-brew compatibility skips. Both new callback regressions passed within the full run.\n- Full UI suite: 77/77 passed in one clean run without retries, including the new queued-clear journey.\n- Independent UI rereview and expert code review approved the exact final source. Fresh preferences/cache restored exactly; no real package mutations.\n\n## Scope and merge order\n\nThis fixes clear-before-debounce only. The distinct pre-existing completed-cask-search/same-row stale-table issue remains outside scope.\n\nInitially based on the refactor branch. Retarget this PR to main before merging/deleting its parent branch, then require green CI against the updated base before merging this PR.\n"}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA /private/tmp/cakebrew-delivery.1XpoA7/search-refactor.md\nA /private/tmp/cakebrew-delivery.1XpoA7/localization.md\nA /private/tmp/cakebrew-delivery.1XpoA7/search-clear.md\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1788830387230,"completed_at_ms":1788830391976}}
